# PROPOSAL — NOT APPLIED. DO NOT auto-apply / auto-deploy. Orchestrator deploys after owner review.
#
# WHAT: Re-point boiler watchdog (id 1789400001001) from the WRONG signal
# binary_sensor.boiler_alarm (ecoNET curr.alarmOutput) to the ONLY true fault
# indicator: sensor.boiler_mode == 'Авария' (ecoNET mode 9). Notification-only.
#
# WHY: R0 audit (docs/audit/ECONET_ALARMOUTPUT_SEMANTICS.md,
# BOILER_WATCHDOG_RUNTIME_2026-07-17.md) proved curr.alarmOutput asserts routinely
# during NORMAL summer operation (Догорание idle while the electric ТЭН heats DHW).
# The old watchdog fired ~10 false alarms/day (re-armed on every unavailable→on
# WiFi flap) and sent the misleading "погас огонь / нет тепла" text. mode==Авария
# never occurred once in 6 days. This fix eliminates the false positives while
# still catching a genuine controller fault.
#
# DESIGN (all notification-only — ZERO device commands):
#   - alarm  : state sensor.boiler_mode -> 'Авария', for 00:05:00 (rides WiFi flaps).
#   - recover: state sensor.boiler_mode  from 'Авария', for 00:02:00.
#   - Dedup / cooldown: alarm branch gated on this.attributes.last_triggered — one
#     alert, then at most one per 60 min while the fault persists/flaps (no helper
#     write, so the zero-command contract holds).
#   - Recovery: only when leaving Авария to a REAL mode (not unavailable/unknown/
#     Авария) AND the automation has fired before (best-effort episode gate without
#     a write-latch).
#   - Sensor loss (unknown/unavailable) NEVER emits the fault alarm: the alarm
#     trigger only reacts to `to: Авария`; the recover branch is blocked when the
#     new state is unavailable/unknown.
#   - Keeps the ha_startup_grace guard. 24/7 (a fault matters at night too).
#   - ONLY action: telegram_bot.send_message (chat_id 100000000). Verified by
#     tests/test_boiler_watchdog.py.
#
# OVERLAP WITH 1779000001002 («🔥 Котёл: уведомления о режиме и уставках»):
#   1779000001002 also has an Авария sub-clause, BUT it (a) fires only 07:00–22:00,
#   (b) is suppressed on unavailable→Авария (the common ecoNET flap entry),
#   (c) has no persistence reminder and no recovery-from-Авария message. So it does
#   NOT reliably cover Авария; in practice the flap-suppression means it rarely
#   fires on a real fault. This watchdog is the authoritative, 24/7, flap-robust
#   Авария path. To make it the SOLE path, the orchestrator MAY (optional, separate
#   one-liner, NOT in this patch per the "touch only the watchdog" constraint)
#   drop `or to_val == 'Авария'` from 1779000001002's mode branch. Left untouched
#   here so this patch changes only automation 1789400001001.
#
# TARGET FILE ON HA: /config/automations.yaml (fetched read-only via `sudo cat`).
# CHANGES: replaces the existing 1789400001001 block in place. NO other automation
# (incl. 1779000001002) is modified. id 1789400001001 preserved & unique.
#
# APPLY (after review, from a dir whose automations.yaml == the fetched original):
#   patch -p1 --dry-run < docs/audit/boiler_watchdog_fix.patch   # verify
#   patch -p1          < docs/audit/boiler_watchdog_fix.patch     # apply to working copy
#   # on HA: back up first, deploy the patched file, then:
#   #   POST /api/config/core/check_config      # sanity BEFORE reload
#   #   POST /api/services/automation/reload     # NO HA restart needed
#
# ROLLBACK:
#   patch -p1 -R < docs/audit/boiler_watchdog_fix.patch          # revert working copy
#   # on HA: restore the backup, then POST /api/services/automation/reload
#
